# ============================================================================
# Notes:
#
# 1. Environment Variables:
#    - Always use .env.example as a template
#    - Never commit actual .env files with real credentials
#
# 2. Large Files:
#    - ML models should be stored separately or downloaded on-demand
#    - Consider using Git LFS for files > 50MB if needed
#
# 3. Reports:
#    - Generated reports are gitignored to avoid bloating the repo
#    - Use cloud storage or artifact storage for important reports
#
# 4. To override rules:
#    - Use !pattern to un-ignore specific files
#    - Example: !important_config.env
#
# 5. Verify ignore rules:
#    - git check-ignore -v <file> to see which rule applies
#    - git status --ignored to see ignored files
#
# ============================================================================
